import{_ as t,o,c as r,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 515 | Quest Sediment Domain | The Civilizational Error-Correction Project in the Quest Domain","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 515 | Quest Sediment Domain | The Civilizational Error-Correction Project in the Quest Domain","no":515,"module":3,"tags":["Quest Sediment Domain","Civilizational Error-Correction","Historical Reversal","Causal Repair","Institutional Improvement"],"related":["89-Time-Paradox Prevention Mechanism","83-Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervention Maxim","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0515_模块3-求索域文明纠错工程.md","filePath":"en/0515_模块3-求索域文明纠错工程.md"}'),n={name:"en/0515_模块3-求索域文明纠错工程.md"};function a(s,e,l,c,h,d){return o(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="entry-515-quest-sediment-domain-the-civilizational-error-correction-project-in-the-quest-domain" tabindex="-1">Entry 515 | Quest Sediment Domain | The Civilizational Error-Correction Project in the Quest Domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-515-quest-sediment-domain-the-civilizational-error-correction-project-in-the-quest-domain" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 515 | Quest Sediment Domain | The Civilizational Error-Correction Project in the Quest Domain&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain | Benchmark base: Documents 89, 83, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-give-civilization-a-second-chance-but-without-touching-real-history" tabindex="-1">Introduction: give civilization a &quot;second chance,&quot; but without touching real history <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-give-civilization-a-second-chance-but-without-touching-real-history" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: give civilization a &quot;second chance,&quot; but without touching real history&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilization also makes mistakes. A civilization may choose the wrong direction at a crossroads, and from then slide toward predation, toward closure, toward self-destruction. In real history, once such a mistake is made, the price is the lives of tens of thousands of beings. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Quest Sediment Domain provides a more responsible approach: <strong>in isolated space, re-enact that wrong crossroads</strong> — without touching real history, only in an instance let Myriad Ranks see &quot;what if the other road had been chosen.&quot; This is the civilizational error-correction project. Six top-level axioms are its highest principles: anti-predation axiom does not use error-correction projects to plunder real history; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires error-correction results face Myriad Ranks; collective ascension axiom requires error correction not abandon the civilization that once erred; causal self-discipline axiom requires error correction strictly isolated, not disturbing real causality; law-first axiom requires error-correction process stable and recalculable. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-four-kinds-of-objects-of-the-error-correction-project" tabindex="-1">I. Four Kinds of Objects of the Error-Correction Project <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-four-kinds-of-objects-of-the-error-correction-project" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Four Kinds of Objects of the Error-Correction Project&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Typical Problem</th><th>Correction Method</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Institutional error</td><td>Chose predatory distribution, leading to class solidification</td><td>In the instance rerun &quot;if symbiotic distribution had been chosen&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Technical error</td><td>Developed irreversible destructive technology</td><td>In the instance rerun &quot;if sustainable technology had been developed first&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Cultural error</td><td>Defined an ethnic group as &quot;enemy&quot;</td><td>In the instance rerun &quot;if Myriad-Rank republicanism had been the base&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Individual error</td><td>A certain strong one swallowed by the shortcut inner-demon</td><td>In the instance rerun &quot;if he had taken the dual route then&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Four object types cover all common errors from macro institutions to micro individuals.</p><h2 id="ii-three-iron-laws-of-error-correction" tabindex="-1">II. Three Iron Laws of Error Correction <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-three-iron-laws-of-error-correction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Three Iron Laws of Error Correction&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Do not move real causality</strong>: all error correction done in isolated space; do not return to the real timeline to change history;</li><li><strong>Do not decide for real civilizations</strong>: error-correction output is &quot;another possibility&quot; textbook; whether the real civilization borrows it is its own decision;</li><li><strong>Do not humiliate those who erred</strong>: error correction&#39;s purpose is learning, not criticism; historically predatory strong ones in instances are also treated as &quot;people who took the wrong road,&quot; not demonized.</li></ol><h2 id="iii-error-correction-project-and-time-paradox-prevention" tabindex="-1">III. Error-Correction Project and Time-Paradox Prevention <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-error-correction-project-and-time-paradox-prevention" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Error-Correction Project and Time-Paradox Prevention&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The error-correction project most easily triggers the controversy: &quot;are you doing time travel and rewriting history?&quot; The answer is no. It strictly follows Document 89&#39;s time-paradox prevention mechanism:</p><ul><li>Only build instances in isolated space; do not touch the real timeline;</li><li>All results in the instance returned as &quot;abstract knowledge&quot;;</li><li>Any temptation to &quot;go back and save people&quot; is explicitly rejected — the past cannot be changed, but lessons can be propagated.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-the-historical-reversal-narrative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With the &quot;Historical Reversal&quot; Narrative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-the-historical-reversal-narrative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With the &quot;Historical Reversal&quot; Narrative&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In predatory-school systems, strong ones often rely on &quot;going back to the past&quot; or &quot;starting over a lifetime&quot; to correct errors; essentially using time as a personal cheat. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s error-correction project is the opposite: <strong>do not allow anyone to really go back and change history</strong>; only allow learning in instances. This is not insufficient technology, but a matter of principle — if rewriting history is allowed, the causal chain will be torn forever; civilization will fall into a new predation where &quot;whoever is strong can rewrite the past.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-long-term-tracking-of-the-error-correction-project" tabindex="-1">V. Long-Term Tracking of the Error-Correction Project <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-long-term-tracking-of-the-error-correction-project" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Long-Term Tracking of the Error-Correction Project&quot;">​</a></h2><p>One error-correction project closing does not mean the problem is really solved. The Alaya Network will continue tracking that plane for fifty reality years after closure: see whether the error-correction output scheme is really adopted, whether adoption produces new unexpected problems, whether correction is needed. This long-term tracking is the extension of Quest-Domain and Acceleration-Domain collaboration — the Acceleration Domain is responsible for quickly producing schemes; the Quest Domain is responsible for slowly validating schemes; the tracking mechanism is responsible for confirming the scheme still holds on long time scales. Error correction without tracking is just another form of ad hoc decision.</p><h3 id="ethical-bottom-line-of-the-error-correction-project" tabindex="-1">Ethical Bottom Line of the Error-Correction Project <a class="header-anchor" href="#ethical-bottom-line-of-the-error-correction-project" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Ethical Bottom Line of the Error-Correction Project&quot;">​</a></h3><p>No matter how useful the error-correction project is, there are three things that cannot be touched: cannot return to the real timeline to save specific people (causality is irreversible); cannot decide &quot;the other road&quot; for real civilizations (the right to choose is the civilization&#39;s own); cannot treat error-correction conclusions as a trial of historical figures (review is not a court). Three bottom lines written into the Quest-Domain operation procedure; before any error-correction project starts, signature confirmation required. Error correction without bottom lines will itself become a new historical intervention.</p><h3 id="relationship-between-the-error-correction-project-and-real-time" tabindex="-1">Relationship Between the Error-Correction Project and Real Time <a class="header-anchor" href="#relationship-between-the-error-correction-project-and-real-time" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Relationship Between the Error-Correction Project and Real Time&quot;">​</a></h3><p>It must be re-emphasized: the error-correction project does not touch real history. If a plane really suffered civilizational collapse, Heng Yuan Zhou will not go back and stop that collapse — what already happened, let it happen. What the error-correction project does is: distill the lessons of that collapse, so other planes need not repeat it. This is the strict boundary of the causal self-discipline axiom: we learn the past, but do not tamper with it.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: one error-correction project avoids the same mistake recurring on other planes; what is saved is Myriad Ranks&#39; lives</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the error-correction project itself is anti-predation — it explicitly displays predatory choices as &quot;error cases&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s protagonist corrects errors through rebirth/retrogression; supporting roles do not have this right; Heng Yuan Zhou writes error correction into a Myriad-Ranks-shared textbook</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: four error-correction object types cover macro institutions and micro individuals, no racial limit</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: error-correction process, instance standards, case library all public; any plane may submit its own error-correction needs</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilization does not need a god to rewrite the past; what civilization needs is to read the past thoroughly. The Quest Sediment Domain&#39;s civilizational error-correction project turns &quot;what if then&quot; into a lesson Myriad Ranks can repeatedly practice, not some protagonist&#39;s private privilege. This is the causal self-discipline axiom&#39;s most thorough response to &quot;historical reversal.&quot;</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./89-时间悖论防控机制.html">89-Time-Paradox Prevention Mechanism</a> · <a href="./83-先观测后有限干涉准则.html">83-Observe-First-Then-Limited-Intervention Maxim</a> · <a href="./04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li></ul>',26)])])}const m=t(n,[["render",a]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
